AERA Recovery — OPPO R9 Plusm A (r9plus) port
=============================================

This repository contains original research, documentation, and device
configuration produced for the AERA Recovery project.

Third-party components and their origins
----------------------------------------

AERA Recovery
  https://github.com/AERA-Recovery
  AERA is built on AOSP Recovery, TWRP, OrangeFox, and LineageOS work.
  See the upstream repositories and their NOTICE/COPYING files.

TeamWin Recovery Project (TWRP)
  https://github.com/TeamWin
  The R9Plus recovery.fstab / twrp.flags baseline is derived from the
  TipzTeam recovery_device_oppo_thortanium tree:
  https://codeberg.org/TipzTeam/recovery_device_oppo_thortanium

LineageOS
  https://github.com/LineageOS
  The 4.9.337 recovery kernel, FDT, and OPPO recovery certificate were
  extracted from the public LineageOS 22.1 R9Plus release:
  https://github.com/BlueyfishReleases/R9Plus

CyanogenMod / wuxianlin R9Plus device tree
  https://github.com/wuxianlin/android_device_oppo_r9plus
  Used for codename verification, partition table, keylayout, and
  CM14.1 baseline evidence.

Linux kernel
  The prebuilt kernel is GPL-2.0. Its source is:
  https://github.com/blueyfish/android_kernel_oppo_msm8937
  branch lineage-22.1.

OPPO boot certificate
  The 1,280-byte DER blob is extracted from the public LineageOS R9Plus
  recovery image and is included only to reproduce the boot image layout
  required by this device's aboot.

No OPPO proprietary firmware or full ROM is redistributed here.

The original documentation and device-tree configuration in this repository
are released under GPL-3.0-or-later. Upstream files retain their original
licenses and copyright notices.
